# ---------------- IMPORT LIBRARIES ----------------
import pandas as pd
import numpy as np
import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
import seaborn as sns
import plotly.express as px
import plotly.graph_objects as go
from plotly.subplots import make_subplots

# ---------------- SETTINGS ----------------
sns.set_theme(style="darkgrid")
plt.rcParams["figure.figsize"] = (10,6)

colors = ["#1F77B4", "#FF7F0E", "#2CA02C", "#D62728", "#9467BD"]

# ---------------- LOAD DATA ----------------
df = pd.read_csv("sales_data (3).csv")

print("Dataset Shape:", df.shape)
print(df.head())

# ==========================================================
# 1. BAR CHART (Category Sales)
# ==========================================================
if "Category" in df.columns and "Total_Sales" in df.columns:
    plt.figure(figsize=(8,5))
    sns.barplot(data=df, x="Category", y="Total_Sales", palette=colors)
    plt.title("Sales by Category")
    plt.xticks(rotation=45)
    plt.show()

# ==========================================================
# 2. LINE CHART (Monthly Sales)
# ==========================================================
if "Month" in df.columns and "Total_Sales" in df.columns:
    monthly = df.groupby("Month")["Total_Sales"].sum().reset_index()

    plt.figure(figsize=(10,5))
    sns.lineplot(data=monthly,
                 x="Month",
                 y="Total_Sales",
                 marker="o",
                 color=colors[0])
    plt.title("Monthly Sales Trend")
    plt.show()

# ==========================================================
# 3. HISTOGRAM
# ==========================================================
if "Total_Sales" in df.columns:
    plt.figure(figsize=(8,5))
    sns.histplot(df["Total_Sales"],
                 bins=20,
                 kde=True,
                 color=colors[2])
    plt.title("Sales Distribution")
    plt.show()

# ==========================================================
# 4. BOXPLOT
# ==========================================================
if "Category" in df.columns and "Total_Sales" in df.columns:
    plt.figure(figsize=(8,5))
    sns.boxplot(data=df,
                x="Category",
                y="Total_Sales",
                palette=colors)
    plt.title("Category vs Sales")
    plt.xticks(rotation=45)
    plt.show()

# ==========================================================
# 5. HEATMAP
# ==========================================================
plt.figure(figsize=(8,6))
sns.heatmap(df.corr(numeric_only=True),
            annot=True,
            cmap="coolwarm")
plt.title("Correlation Heatmap")
plt.show()

# ==========================================================
# INTERACTIVE PLOTLY PIE CHART
# ==========================================================
if "Category" in df.columns and "Total_Sales" in df.columns:
    pie = px.pie(df,
                 names="Category",
                 values="Total_Sales",
                 title="Sales Distribution by Category",
                 color_discrete_sequence=px.colors.qualitative.Set2)
    pie.show()

# ==========================================================
# INTERACTIVE PROFESSIONAL DASHBOARD
# ==========================================================
fig = make_subplots(
    rows=2,
    cols=2,
    subplot_titles=[
        "Category Sales",
        "Monthly Sales",
        "Sales Distribution",
        "Top Products"
    ]
)

# Bar Chart
if "Category" in df.columns and "Total_Sales" in df.columns:
    cat = df.groupby("Category")["Total_Sales"].sum()

    fig.add_trace(
        go.Bar(
            x=cat.index,
            y=cat.values,
            marker_color="royalblue",
            name="Category Sales"
        ),
        row=1,
        col=1
    )

# Line Chart
if "Month" in df.columns and "Total_Sales" in df.columns:
    monthly = df.groupby("Month")["Total_Sales"].sum()

    fig.add_trace(
        go.Scatter(
            x=monthly.index,
            y=monthly.values,
            mode="lines+markers",
            line=dict(color="green"),
            name="Monthly Sales"
        ),
        row=1,
        col=2
    )

# Histogram
if "Total_Sales" in df.columns:
    fig.add_trace(
        go.Histogram(
            x=df["Total_Sales"],
            marker_color="orange",
            name="Sales Distribution"
        ),
        row=2,
        col=1
    )

# Top Products
if "Product" in df.columns and "Total_Sales" in df.columns:
    top = df.groupby("Product")["Total_Sales"].sum().nlargest(10)

    fig.add_trace(
        go.Bar(
            x=top.index,
            y=top.values,
            marker_color="crimson",
            name="Top Products"
        ),
        row=2,
        col=2
    )

fig.update_layout(
    title="Professional Sales Dashboard",
    height=800,
    width=1200,
    template="plotly_dark",
    showlegend=False
)

fig.show()
